From ca3b710a0fd3d456dfd4b23acca9092b910af595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnSnow <110465696+JohnSnow14284@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 09:55:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] Add far-vehicle render data and resilience

Bump protocol to v7 and add support for vehicle render payloads. VehicleSnapshot now carries compressed renderData with size limits and safe (de)serialization. Player tracking gains vehicleRenderData + revision counters. Server caches/compresses entity NBT (skips oversized data) and only sends render data to clients when it changes. Client renderer loads NBT into proxy entities, guards rendering with try/catch, and disables/replaces failing proxies while tracking revisions to avoid repeated work. Added logging and several defensive checks to prevent oversize or invalid data and reduce unnecessary network traffic.
